WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.213
Two ideas hold the design together.

2
00:00:02.213 --> 00:00:04.112
The first is idempotency.

3
00:00:04.112 --> 00:00:06.133
The key isn't a Microsoft feature;

4
00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:10.325
it's a promise the downstream system
makes to do the work once per key.

5
00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:15.852
That matters because the same task can
arrive twice: the extension may retry its

6
00:00:15.852 --> 00:00:17.778
call, a workflow can be rerun,

7
00:00:17.778 --> 00:00:21.462
and Book 03 resumes a partial
leaver where it stopped.

8
00:00:21.462 --> 00:00:25.683
The second is the registry: one
reviewed entry per integration,

9
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:28.524
holding every value the deployment needs.

10
00:00:28.524 --> 00:00:31.387
Its extension settings
have sensible defaults,

11
00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:34.800
and the builder refuses anything
outside Learn's ranges.
